# Production dependencies and first-party sources allowed to reach the network.
# Owned by .claude/scripts/check-no-network-egress.sh, whose header owns this format; every
# entry is an owner decision under CLAUDE.md § Hard constraints.
better-sqlite3 a native addon (binding.gyp, prebuilt .node binaries) embedding SQLite in-process for @cram/index (#11, docs/adr/0004-storage.md); it exposes no socket API and opens no connection
node-addon-api better-sqlite3's C++ header dependency; flagged for maintainer scripts under tools/ that spawn processes and are never loaded at runtime (its main entry, index.js, loads only path and its package.json)
unpdf bundles pdf.js, which @cram/ingest reads PDF decks with (#9, packages/ingest/src/adapters/pdf/ingest-pdf.ts); its fetch and XMLHttpRequest sites serve URL-sourced documents and URL-valued options, and the adapter passes only bytes and no URL (packages/ingest/src/adapters/pdf/ingest-pdf.test.ts refuses any request made while a deck is read)
onnxruntime-node a native addon (prebuilt bin/napi-v6/<platform>/onnxruntime_binding.node) running the encoder roles in-process for @cram/gateway (#66, docs/adr/0003-model-roles-and-backends.md § Decision (c)), from local paths only (§ Decision (i)); flagged for script/install-utils.js, which its postinstall script/install.js runs to fetch the linux-x64 CUDA provider from NuGet and which pnpm-workspace.yaml's allowBuilds keeps from running, and for script/build.js, the from-source cmake driver behind its build npm scripts, which nothing runs; its runtime entry (dist/) opens no connection
global-agent onnxruntime-node's proxy bootstrap, required only by its script/install.js, which pnpm-workspace.yaml's allowBuilds keeps from running; nothing loaded at runtime requires it
@napi-rs/canvas the canvas unpdf's renderPageAsImage draws on, for @cram/ingest's stored slide images (#107, docs/adr/0006-image-only-slides.md § Decision (c), A7); flagged for load-image.js, which requires http and https only for loadImage given a URL, and for js-binding.js, which runs ldd --version through child_process on Linux to choose its glibc or musl binary; pdf.js reaches it only through createCanvas and the DOMMatrix, ImageData and Path2D constructors (packages/ingest/src/adapters/pdf/ingest-pdf.test.ts refuses any request made while a deck is read and rendered); no install script
@napi-rs/canvas-darwin-arm64 @napi-rs/canvas's prebuilt Skia binary (skia.darwin-arm64.node) for the development machine, flagged by the native arm; its sbom.cdx.json lists no HTTP or TLS client
@napi-rs/canvas-win32-x64-msvc @napi-rs/canvas's prebuilt Skia binary (skia.win32-x64-msvc.node, with icudtl.dat) for the Windows target, flagged by the native arm; its sbom.cdx.json lists no HTTP or TLS client
@napi-rs/canvas-linux-x64-gnu @napi-rs/canvas's prebuilt Skia binary (skia.linux-x64-gnu.node) for CI's ubuntu-latest runner, flagged by the native arm; its sbom.cdx.json lists no HTTP or TLS client
apps/server/src/server.ts the app's listener (createServer), bound to LOOPBACK_ADDRESS (docs/adr/0002-deployables.md § Decision (d)); it accepts connections and opens none, and apps/server/src/server.test.ts's loopback test holds the bind
apps/server/src/server-fixture.ts the server tests' fixture, outside the .test. naming the census skips; its send helper fixes the request host to 127.0.0.1, and only apps/server's *.test.ts files import it
apps/web/src/main.tsx binds the browser's fetch into ApiClient, whose requests resolve against document.baseURI, the loopback server that served the page (apps/web/src/api/api-client.ts)
packages/gateway/src/adapters/openai-http/openai-http-generator.ts the generator's HTTP adapter (docs/adr/0003-model-roles-and-backends.md § Decision (c)); it posts to the configured endpoint, which LoopbackEndpoint in packages/gateway/src/role-config.ts restricts to loopback hosts (packages/gateway/src/role-config.test.ts refuses a LAN and a 0.0.0.0 endpoint)
